# H-eigenstate cultivation (protocol shape): the raw physical magic state starts in
# T-form (T is the gate set's only single-qubit non-Clifford) and is Clifford-ALIGNED
# onto the Hadamard axis before the checks:
#     |H> = (H S H) T H |0>      Bloch (1/sqrt2, 0, 1/sqrt2), the +1 eigenstate of H.
# Each round measures logical H via a Hadamard test (ancilla |+>, CH onto the data,
# MX ancilla). Because the data is an H-EIGENSTATE, the prep-T's folded magic axis and
# the CH's folded magic axes COINCIDE (all X_d in the input frame) -> commuting magic,
# chi = 2 (the noiseless ancillas never entangle: CH|+>|H> = |+>|H>), and every check
# detector is noiselessly deterministic (postselectable). Feeding the UNALIGNED T-state
# into CH instead is non-commuting magic and rejects -- the class boundary enforces the
# protocol's alignment requirement.
# Noise before each CH forces error-carrying shots through the general (CH-class) path.
H 0
T 0
H 0
S 0
H 0
# round 1
H 1
X_ERROR(0.001) 0 1
Z_ERROR(0.001) 0
CH 1 0
MX 1
DETECTOR rec[-1]
# round 2
H 2
X_ERROR(0.001) 0 2
Z_ERROR(0.001) 0
CH 2 0
MX 2
DETECTOR rec[-1]
# round 3
H 3
X_ERROR(0.001) 0 3
Z_ERROR(0.001) 0
CH 3 0
MX 3
DETECTOR rec[-1]
# the payload: the cultivated H-eigenstate's Bloch vector (1/sqrt2, 0, 1/sqrt2)
PAULI_EXPECTATION(0) X0
PAULI_EXPECTATION(1) Z0
